  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem ahip-demo-disability-codes</b></p><a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes\"> </a><a name=\"hcahip-demo-disability-codes\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #d9e0e7; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Language: en</p></div><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/us/demographic-collect/CodeSystem/ahip-demo-disability-codes</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">HEAR<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-HEAR\"> </a></td><td>Hearing</td><td>Deafness or serious difficulty hearing because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">SEEI<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-SEEI\"> </a></td><td>Seeing (even when wearing glasses)</td><td>Blindness or serious difficulty seeing, even when wearing glasses, because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">WALK<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-WALK\"> </a></td><td>Walking or climbing stairs</td><td>Serious difficulty walking or climbing stairs because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">CONC<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-CONC\"> </a></td><td>Concentrating, remembering, or making decisions</td><td>Serious difficulty concentrating, remembering, or making decisions because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">DRES<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-DRES\"> </a></td><td>Dressing or bathing</td><td>Difficulty dressing or bathing because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">COOK<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-COOK\"> </a></td><td>Cooking for oneself</td><td>Difficulty cooking for oneself because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">FEED<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-FEED\"> </a></td><td>Feeding oneself</td><td>Difficulty feeding oneself because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">TOIL<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-TOIL\"> </a></td><td>Using the toilet</td><td>Difficulty using the toilet because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ERRA<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-ERRA\"> </a></td><td>Doing errands alone, such as shopping or visiting a doctor’s office</td><td>Difficulty doing errands alone, such as shopping or visiting a doctor's office, because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">COMM<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-COMM\"> </a></td><td>Communicating or being understood using your usual language</td><td>Difficulty communicating or being understood using one's usual language because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">UNDE<a name=\"ahip-demo-disability-codes-UNDE\"> </a></td><td>Understanding when someone speaks in your usual language</td><td>Difficulty understanding when someone speaks in one's usual language because of a physical or mental health condition.</td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
